<title>KAZAKHSTAN: TABLE-Kazakh 6-mth T-bill yield rises to 16.24 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Kazakh 6-mth T-bill yield rises to 16.24 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month MKM discount Treasury bills rose to 16.24 at an auction on August 4 from 14.96 at the last auction on July 21, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   Aug 4		July 21</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ46K0502984     KZ462201981</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  600		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	 1,818		1,677</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 600		  600</p>
<p> Average price			 92.49 pct	  93.04</p>
<p> Average yield			 16.24		14.96</p>
<p> Tenor				   182 days	   182 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Feb 5, 1998	Jan 22, 1998</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509 410</p>
